.TH geectl-request-add-comment 1  "geectl-request-add-comment 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-add\-comment \- Comment on a submit request, optionally as a reply to another comment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request add\-comment\fR [\fB\-\-parent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-body\fR> <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Comment on a submit request, optionally as a reply to another comment
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-body\fR \fI<BODY>\fR
The comment text. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: the body may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-parent\fR \fI<PARENT>\fR
The comment being replied to, when this is a reply
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The request id
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
